{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3522","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3522","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3522\",\"parent_revision\":\"fdc0443edda1d4207bcd6c2731d2b9aef657b2955cb588475a2f3611e0b63525\",\"root_revision\":\"fdc0443edda1d4207bcd6c2731d2b9aef657b2955cb588475a2f3611e0b63525\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-13\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`.claude/agents/research-backlink-detector.md` exists and is documented as the owner of reciprocal cross-reference rows: `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/cross-reference-format.md` assigns forward links to `@research-cross-referencer` and reciprocal rows to `@research-backlink-detector`, and `entry-template.md` repeats that split.\\n\\n`.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` never spawns it. Grepping the skill directory finds `@research-backlink-detector` only in those two prose references, never in a dispatch block, a mode's numbered flow, or any Mermaid node. The Default, Batch, and Rerun fan-outs spawn `@research-insight-extractor`, `@research-utilization-assessor`, and `@research-cross-referencer` and stop there.\\n\\nThis is the same orphan class as `entry-review-rubric.md` before PR #3521 \u2014 an artifact documented as part of the workflow with no runtime caller.\\n\\nConsequence observed while wiring Entry Review in PR #3521: because nothing spawns the detector, reciprocity is only ever restored by the deterministic `validate_research.py check-backlinks --fix` pass in Post-Actions step 2. Any audit of cross-reference symmetry that runs before Post-Actions sees a vault that is asymmetric by construction \u2014 the cross-referencer has just added forward links with no reciprocal rows. PR #3521 works around this by running the Post-Actions step 2 repair at the start of its Entry Review step. That workaround is correct but it means two agents' worth of documented responsibility is being carried by one script, and the detector agent is dead weight in the repo.\\n\\nDecide and then make the repo say the same thing in both places: either spawn `@research-backlink-detector` in the analysis fan-out so the documented ownership is real, or delete the agent and rewrite `cross-reference-format.md` and `entry-template.md` to name the `check-backlinks --fix` pass as the owner of reciprocal rows. If the detector is spawned, PR #3521's repair-before-review step can likely be dropped.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the workaround and its reasoning are in PR #3521's description under \\\"Reciprocity is repaired before review, not after\\\".\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Independent review of PR #3521 (Entry Review wiring)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-13\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"63f47745d8295ac28fca94d3f72f263b680fb87961a16d37892ac3cea602ef94\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUPu7Lg\"}"}